avy podium of board-marked concrete with fieldstone set into it, a glazed upper floor under five parallel brick barrel vaults separated by concrete ribs, the vault bands projecting past both long faces as shading eaves, a concrete balcony beam round the upper floor, an open stair up the front, and the water tank standing alone on two concrete legs beside the house) and interiors (double-height hall, floating stair, brick vaults over the upper rooms). Rounds so far: 1 massing; 2 vault ribs added between the five bands; 3 denser fieldstone inclusions, a longer front stair, arched glass heads under each vault end. This pass, against the frontal street photograph: the podium is two bands - a board-marked concrete beam over a rough fieldstone wall - where it had been a concrete block speckled with 230 stones too small to read at this voxel (they are gone: the stone is the wall); the vaults' brick in tan-brown, not tile red; the water tower a 4.4 m concrete cube on two 1.3 m piers at its outer edges with the open gap between (it had been a thin 1.6 m slab on two 1 m legs); the carport an open white slab on slim posts with a dark soffit instead of a solid white block; grasses and shrubs along the podium's foot and a path of steps to the stair. Still guessed: all dimensions (from storey and door heights), the site slope (drawn flat), the stair and tank positions relative to the house, the pool and trees on the north side, the planting. The south front is taken as the street. The house is placed no closer than its town (Cordoba)."}